ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE ACT ON THE SECURING, MANAGEMENT AND USE OF MARINE AND FISHERIES BIORESOURCES

CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on the Securing, Management and Use of Marine and Fisheries Bioresources and matters necessary for its enforcement.

CHAPTER II MASTER PLAN FOR THE MANAGEMENT OF MARINE AND FISHERIES BIORESOURCES, ETC.

Article 2 (Matters to Be Surveyed concerning Marine and Fisheries Bioresources)
(1) Basic surveys under Article 7 (1) of the Act on the Securing, Management and Use of Marine and Fisheries Bioresources (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") shall cover the following matters:
1. The status and habitats of marine and fisheries bioresources conserved in situ;
2. The status and habitats of marine and fisheries bioresources conserved ex situ;
3. The status and habitats of overseas marine and fisheries bioresources held in the Republic of Korea;
4. Other matters determined by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries as requiring a survey for the securing, management and use of marine and fisheries bioresources.
(2) Detailed surveys under Article 7 (2) of the Act shall cover the following matters:
1. The status and causes of damage to marine and fisheries bioresources;
2. Methods of restoring damaged marine and fisheries bioresources;
3. The status of marine and fisheries bioresources that are the subject of an international dispute or are highly likely to become the subject of an international dispute;
4. Other matters determined by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries as requiring an urgent survey for the securing, management and use of marine and fisheries bioresources.

Article 3 (Methods and Procedures for Surveys of Marine and Fisheries Bioresources)
(1) Basic and detailed surveys of marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 7 (1) and (2) of the Act shall, in principle, be conducted directly on site, but indirect survey methods, such as remote sensing, literature surveys, or questionnaire surveys, may be used.
(2) When conducting a survey of marine and fisheries bioresources under paragraph (1), the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may request necessary cooperation from the heads of relevant administrative agencies. In such cases, the heads of those agencies shall comply with the request unless there are special circumstances.
(3) Where necessary for a survey of marine and fisheries bioresources under paragraph (1), the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may designate marine and fisheries bioresource surveyors from among relevant public officials, local experts, or persons with extensive knowledge and experience in fields related to marine and fisheries bioresources.
(4) Matters necessary for survey methods, the deployment of marine and fisheries bioresource surveyors, and related matters under paragraphs (1) through (3) shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries.

Article 4 (Master Plan for the Management of Marine and Fisheries Bioresources)
(1) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 8 (2) 11 of the Act means matters concerning publicity and education regarding marine and fisheries bioresources.
(2) When the master plan for the management of marine and fisheries bioresources is finalized pursuant to Article 8 (5) of the Act, the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall publicly announce it on the website of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries.
(3) "Minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 8 (7) of the Act means the matters referred to in Article 8 (2) 5 through 11 of the Act.

Article 5 (Surveys and Listing of Marine and Fisheries Bioresources)
(1) When preparing a list of marine and fisheries bioresources pursuant to Article 9 (3) of the Act, the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall prepare a list including the names, scientific names, habitats, collectors, places of collection, and other relevant particulars of the marine and fisheries bioresources.
(2) When entering marine and fisheries bioresources in the list for conservation and management of marine and fisheries bioresources pursuant to Article 9 (4) of the Act, the head of a responsible agency for marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 17 (1) of the Act shall ensure that the following matters are included:
1. The resource identification number of the marine and fisheries bioresources;
2. The grade of the marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 10 (1) of the Act;
3. The method of conservation of the marine and fisheries bioresources;
4. The year in which conservation of the marine and fisheries bioresources began and the conservation period;
5. Other matters deemed necessary by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries for the efficient conservation and management of marine and fisheries bioresources.
(3) Details necessary for preparing lists of marine and fisheries bioresources and entering them in the conservation and management list under paragraphs (1) and (2) shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries.

Article 6 (Analysis and Evaluation of Marine and Fisheries Bioresources)
(1) Items for the analysis and evaluation of marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 10 (1) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. Basic information, such as the names, scientific names, and habitats of the marine and fisheries bioresources;
2. Genetic characteristics, such as genomes, transcriptomes, and proteomes;
3. Matters necessary for the conservation of marine and fisheries bioresources, such as growth and production;
4. Matters necessary for the management of marine and fisheries bioresources, such as diseases and resistance;
5. Matters necessary for utilization, such as the industrial usefulness of marine and fisheries bioresources;
6. Other matters deemed necessary by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries for the management and utilization of marine and fisheries bioresources.
(2) When the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries assigns a grade to marine and fisheries bioresources pursuant to Article 10 (1) of the Act, the Minister shall publicly announce that fact on the website of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries.
(3) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries deems it necessary to analyze or evaluate marine and fisheries bioresources or assign grades to them pursuant to Article 10 (1) of the Act, the Minister may request relevant institutions, organizations, or experts in the field to submit data or opinions or provide other necessary cooperation.
(4) The Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may determine and publicly notify details necessary for the procedures and methods for analyzing and evaluating marine and fisheries bioresources and assigning grades to them under paragraphs (1) through (3), and related matters.

Article 7 (Procedures for Permission to Acquire Marine and Fisheries Bioresources)
(1) A foreigner or international organization (hereinafter referred to as "foreigners, etc.") seeking permission to acquire marine and fisheries bioresources under the main clause of Article 11 (1) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries an application for permission to acquire marine and fisheries bioresources in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by a survey plan containing the following matters. Where a person other than a foreign government or international organization applies for permission, the application shall be submitted through the government of the country to which that person belongs.
1. The purpose and subjects of the survey;
2. The methods and means of the survey;
3. Survey personnel;
4. Survey equipment and facilities;
5. The waters to be surveyed;
6. Survey vessels;
7. Matters concerning the reporting and use of survey results;
8. Matters concerning participation by nationals of the Republic of Korea.
(2) Upon receipt of an application for permission under paragraph (1), the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall decide whether to grant permission after consultation with the heads of relevant administrative agencies.
(3) When granting permission under the main clause of Article 11 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall issue to the applicant a permit for acquisition of marine and fisheries bioresources in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries (hereinafter referred to as an "acquisition permit"). The acquisition permit shall contain the following matters:
1. The name, trade name, or personal name of the permit holder;
2. The marine and fisheries bioresources for which permission has been granted;
3. The equipment and facilities for which permission has been granted;
4. The waters for which permission has been granted;
5. The vessels for which permission has been granted;
6. The period of permission;
7. The conditions of permission.
(4) A foreigner, etc. who has obtained permission under the main clause of Article 11 (1) of the Act shall, pursuant to paragraph (4) of that Article, display a flag prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries on the exterior of the vessel for which permission has been granted.

Article 8 (Procedures for Permission for Joint Acquisition of Marine and Fisheries Bioresources)
(1) A person seeking permission for joint acquisition of marine and fisheries bioresources under the main clause of Article 12 (1) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries an application for permission for joint acquisition in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by the following documents:
1. A survey plan containing the matters listed in the subparagraphs of Article 7 (1);
2. Documents concerning delegation, entrustment, contracts, or similar arrangements related to joint acquisition;
3. A plan for the use of the marine and fisheries bioresources to be jointly acquired;
4. Documents containing matters concerning the allocation and handling of acquired marine and fisheries bioresources among the parties participating in joint acquisition.
(2) Article 7 (2) through (4) shall apply mutatis mutandis to permission for joint acquisition under paragraph (1).

Article 9 (Duties of Foreigners, Etc.)
A foreigner, etc. who has obtained permission under the main clause of Article 11 (1) or the main clause of Article 12 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "permission") shall submit the data under Article 13 (3) 1 of the Act to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries within three months from the date on which the period of permission expires: Provided, That where research, development, production, commercial use, or other relevant activities involving the marine and fisheries bioresources end before the period of permission expires, the data shall be submitted within three months from the date on which those activities end.

Article 10 (Conditions of Permission)
The term "conditions, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 15 of the Act means the following matters:
1. Compliance with domestic statutes and regulations, international treaties, and other applicable instruments;
2. Restrictions on the acquisition of marine and fisheries bioresources, such as a prohibition on acquisition after sunset;
3. The release or other handling of marine and fisheries bioresources captured or collected during acquisition other than those for which permission has been granted;
4. Restrictions on the use of equipment and facilities used to acquire marine and fisheries bioresources;
5. Follow-up management related to the acquisition of marine and fisheries bioresources;
6. Plans for preventive measures and follow-up management to conserve the marine environment;
7. Other matters deemed necessary by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries to conserve marine and fisheries bioresources.

Article 11 (Surveys of Damage to the Diversity of Marine and Fisheries Bioresources)
(1) Surveys under Article 16 (3) of the Act shall, in principle, be conducted directly in the habitat, but indirect survey methods, such as remote sensing, literature surveys, or questionnaire surveys, may be used.
(2) When conducting a survey under paragraph (1), the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries or a specialized institution entrusted with the survey pursuant to Article 16 (3) of the Act may request necessary cooperation from relevant institutions, organizations, or experts.
(3) A specialized institution entrusted with a survey pursuant to Article 16 (3) of the Act shall, upon completing the survey, submit the survey results, including a plan for appropriate measures, to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries within 15 days from the date of completion.

CHAPTER III DESIGNATION AND OPERATION OF RESPONSIBLE AGENCIES FOR MARINE AND FISHERIES BIORESOURCES, ETC.

Article 12 (Designation of Responsible Agencies for Marine and Fisheries Bioresources)
(1) "Institutions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 17 (1) of the Act means the following institutions:
1. The National Institute of Fisheries Science;
2. The National Marine Biodiversity Institute of Korea under the Act on the Establishment and Operation of the National Marine Biodiversity Institute of Korea (hereinafter referred to as the "National Marine Biodiversity Institute of Korea").
(2) When the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries designates a responsible agency for marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 17 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "responsible agency"), the Minister shall publicly announce that fact on the website of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries.
(3) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 17 (2) 9 of the Act means matters concerning technology development and research and development related to marine and fisheries bioresources. <Amended on December 3, 2019>

Article 13 (Operation of Responsible Agencies)
(1) The head of a responsible agency shall secure the facilities and specialized personnel necessary to ensure the diversity of marine and fisheries bioresources and their safe preservation and management and efficient use, for the efficient operation of the responsible agency.
(2) The head of a responsible agency shall submit the following status information to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries by January 31 of each year:
1. The status of preservation of marine and fisheries bioresources;
2. The status of evaluation of marine and fisheries bioresources;
3. The status of distribution of marine and fisheries bioresources;
4. The status of informatization of marine and fisheries bioresources;
5. The progress of other research projects and related activities concerning marine and fisheries bioresources.
(3) To prepare for circumstances that may seriously affect the safety of marine and fisheries bioresources, such as natural disasters, insurrection, or war, the head of a responsible agency shall maintain a close system of cooperation for the collection, preservation, propagation, evaluation, and utilization of marine and fisheries bioresources with deposit, registration and preservation agencies for marine and fisheries bioresources designated pursuant to Article 18(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "deposit, registration and preservation agencies").

Article 14 (Criteria and Procedures for Designation of Deposit, Registration and Preservation Agencies)
(1) The term "facilities and personnel prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 18(1) of the Act means the following facilities and personnel:
1. Possession of equipment and facilities capable of preserving and managing at least 100 specimens of marine and fisheries bioresources on a long-term basis;
2. Personnel falling under either of the following items shall constitute at least one-fifth of all personnel (or one person where the total number of personnel is fewer than five):
(a) Persons holding a master's degree or higher in life sciences or marine life sciences under the National Standard Science and Technology Classification System under Article 27 of the Framework Act on Science and Technology;
(b) Persons who have worked in a related field for at least three years after obtaining a bachelor's degree in life sciences or marine life sciences under the National Standard Science and Technology Classification System under Article 27 of the Framework Act on Science and Technology;
3. Possession of computer equipment, backup facilities, and security facilities for operating a marine and fisheries bioresources information system, and at least one person capable of managing such equipment and facilities.
(2) A person seeking designation as a deposit, registration and preservation agency shall submit to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries an application for designation as a deposit, registration and preservation agency prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by the following documents:
1. Documents proving that the designation criteria in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) have been satisfied;
2. A business plan;
3. Deleted. <March 30, 2021>
(3) Upon receipt of an application under paragraph (2), the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall notify the applicant whether designation is granted within 30 days from the date of receipt of the application; provided that, where there is an unavoidable reason, the period may be extended once by up to 30 days.
(4) Where an application and accompanying documents submitted under paragraph (2) contain defects, such as missing information or documents, the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall set a reasonable period necessary for supplementation and require the applicant to supplement them without delay. In such cases, the time taken for supplementation shall not be included in the period under paragraph (3).
(5) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries extends the period for deciding whether to grant designation pursuant to the proviso to paragraph (3), the Minister shall inform the applicant of the extension and its reasons in a document (including an electronic document).
(6) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries designates a deposit, registration and preservation agency pursuant to paragraph (3), the Minister shall issue to the applicant a certificate of designation as a deposit, registration and preservation agency prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries and give public notice of the designation on the website of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries.
(7) The Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may determine and publicly notify detailed matters necessary for the designation criteria and designation procedures, including applications for designation and public notice, under paragraphs (1) through (6).
(8) The term "matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 18(2)4 of the Act means matters concerning publicity and exhibitions of marine and fisheries bioresources.
(9) The designation period of a deposit, registration and preservation agency shall be three years from the date of designation.
(10) The Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall inform the head of a deposit, registration and preservation agency in advance of the expiration date of the designation period, redesignation procedures, and related matters no later than 90 days before the designation period expires.

Article 15 (Procedures for Redesignation of Deposit, Registration and Preservation Agencies)
(1) A person seeking redesignation as a deposit, registration and preservation agency shall submit to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries, no later than 60 days before the designation period expires, an application for redesignation as a deposit, registration and preservation agency for marine and fisheries bioresources prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by the following documents:
1. Documents proving that the designation criteria in the subparagraphs of Article 14(1) have been satisfied;
2. A business plan (including operating performance before the application for redesignation);
3. A budget operation plan;
4. Deleted. <July 16, 2024>
(2) Article 14(3) through (7) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the procedures for redesignation under paragraph (1). In such cases, "designation" shall be construed as "redesignation."

Article 16 (Revocation of Designation of Deposit, Registration and Preservation Agencies)
(1) The criteria for administrative dispositions against deposit, registration and preservation agencies under Article 19(1) of the Act shall be as prescribed in Attached Table 1.
(2) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries revokes the designation of a deposit, registration and preservation agency pursuant to Article 19(1) of the Act, the Minister shall give public notice of that fact on the website of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries.

Article 17 (Criteria for Distribution Approval)
(1) The criteria for distribution approval for marine and fisheries bioresources under the main clause of Article 20(1) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. None of the grounds for restricting distribution approval in the subparagraphs of Article 20(2) of the Act shall apply;
2. There shall be no impediment to protecting the rights of the right holder of the relevant marine and fisheries bioresources;
3. The applicant shall have facilities, equipment, and other resources for utilizing the relevant marine and fisheries bioresources;
4. Other criteria prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, such as the quantity to be distributed, genetic characteristics, or conservation value, shall be satisfied.
(2) The Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may determine and publicly notify the criteria for the quantities of marine and fisheries bioresources held under Article 20(2)1 of the Act for each species of marine and fisheries bioresources, taking the following matters into consideration:
1. The grade of the marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 10(1) of the Act;
2. The status of ecological preservation of the marine and fisheries bioresources;
3. The academic research value of the marine and fisheries bioresources;
4. The economic utilization value of the marine and fisheries bioresources;
5. Other matters deemed necessary by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries for the preservation and use of marine and fisheries bioresources.
(3) The Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may determine and publicly notify the details of the criteria for distribution approval under paragraph (1).

Article 18 (Procedures for Distribution Approval)
(1) A person seeking distribution approval for marine and fisheries bioresources pursuant to the main clause of Article 20(1) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries an application for distribution approval for marine and fisheries bioresources prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by a list of the marine and fisheries bioresources for which distribution is requested.
(2) Upon receipt of an application under paragraph (1), the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall examine whether the criteria for distribution approval under Article 17(1) are satisfied and notify the applicant whether distribution approval is granted within 30 days from the date of receipt of the application; provided that, where there is an unavoidable reason, the period may be extended once by up to 30 days.
(3) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries decides to grant distribution approval pursuant to paragraph (2), the Minister shall issue to the applicant a certificate of distribution approval for marine and fisheries bioresources prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries.
(4) The Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may determine and publicly notify detailed matters necessary for the procedures and methods for distribution approval under paragraphs (1) and (2), and other related matters.

Article 19 (Criteria and Procedures for Approval of a Change in Use)
(1) The criteria for approval of a change in use under Article 20(3) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. The criteria for distribution approval under Article 17(1) shall be satisfied;
2. The change in use shall not contribute to a reduction of or damage to marine and fisheries bioresources;
3. There shall be reasonable and valid grounds requiring a change in use in light of domestic and foreign patents, papers, research results, and other relevant matters.
(2) A person seeking approval of a change in use pursuant to Article 20(3) of the Act shall apply to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries by submitting an application for approval of a change in use prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by the following documents:
1. Documents proving that the criteria for approval of a change in use in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) have been satisfied;
2. A list of the marine and fisheries bioresources for which approval of a change in use is requested;
3. A plan for using the marine and fisheries bioresources following the change in use;
4. Documents concerning the actual use of the resources for the previous purpose.
(3) Upon receipt of an application under paragraph (2), the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall notify the applicant whether approval of the change in use is granted within 30 days from the date of receipt of the application; provided that, where there is an unavoidable reason, the period may be extended once by up to 30 days.
(4) The Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may determine and publicly notify the details of the criteria for approval of a change in use under paragraphs (1) through (3), and detailed matters necessary for the procedures and methods for approval of a change in use and other related matters.

Article 20 (Revocation of Distribution Approval and Procedures for Return)
(1) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries revokes distribution approval pursuant to Article 21(1) of the Act, the Minister shall notify the person who obtained distribution approval, the responsible agency, and the deposit, registration and preservation agency of that fact.
(2) A person whose distribution approval has been revoked pursuant to Article 21(1) of the Act shall return the marine and fisheries bioresources approved for distribution to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries within 20 days from the date of receipt of the notification under paragraph (1); provided that this shall not apply where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries finds that there is an unavoidable reason making return impossible, such as loss of or damage to the marine and fisheries bioresources.

Article 20-2 (Criteria for Preparing the List of Resources Subject to Approval for Overseas Transfer)
(1) The Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall prepare the list of resources subject to approval for overseas transfer under the main clause of Article 22(1) of the Act, taking the following matters into consideration:
1. The economic, ecological, and academic value of marine and fisheries bioresources;
2. The rarity of populations of marine and fisheries bioresources or the possibility of their decline.
(2) When preparing the list of resources subject to approval for overseas transfer pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may hear the opinions of the heads of responsible agencies and relevant national and public research institutions.

Article 21 (Criteria and Procedures for Approval for Overseas Transfer)
(1) The criteria for approval for overseas transfer of marine and fisheries bioresources under the main clause of Article 22(1) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. The transfer shall not impede the conservation of marine and fisheries bioresources subject to protection under relevant statutes and regulations, including the Conservation and Management of Marine Ecosystems Act;
2. The resources shall not be marine and fisheries bioresources whose overseas transfer is prohibited under domestic statutes and regulations, international treaties, or the like;
3. The resources shall not be marine and fisheries bioresources that pose a risk of harm to the State if transferred overseas;
4. The transfer shall not impede the protection of the rights of persons holding rights to the relevant marine and fisheries bioresources;
5. Other criteria prescribed and publicly notified by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries, including criteria concerning the purpose of transfer, the quantity to be transferred, or genetic characteristics, shall be met.
(2) A person who intends to obtain approval for overseas transfer of marine and fisheries bioresources under the main clause of Article 22(1) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries an application for approval for overseas transfer, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by the following documents: <Amended on December 3, 2019>
1. Documents concerning the list of marine and fisheries bioresources for which approval for overseas transfer is sought, the purposes of transfer, and related matters;
2. Documents concerning management plans, including the places and methods of preservation and management following the overseas transfer of marine and fisheries bioresources.
(3) Upon receiving an application under paragraph (2), the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall examine whether the criteria for approval for overseas transfer under paragraph (1) are met and, after consulting with the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, notify the applicant whether approval is granted within 30 days from the date of receipt of the application: Provided, That, where there are unavoidable grounds, the period may be extended once by up to 30 days.
(4) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries intends to decide whether to grant approval for overseas transfer under paragraph (3), the Minister may hear the opinions of the heads of relevant national or public research institutions or make requests, including requests for the submission of necessary materials.
(5) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries decides to grant approval for overseas transfer, the Minister shall issue to the applicant a certificate of approval for overseas transfer of marine and fisheries bioresources, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries.

Article 22 (Criteria and Procedures for Reporting Overseas Transfers)
(1) The term "marine and fisheries bioresources prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as introduced species" in Article 22(2) of the Act means marine and fisheries bioresources falling under either of the following subparagraphs: <Amended on January 5, 2021>
1. Introduced species brought into the Republic of Korea from abroad;
2. Improved varieties for which the period of protection of rights, including patent rights, has expired under relevant statutes and regulations.
(2) The criteria for reporting overseas transfers of marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 22(2) of the Act shall be the criteria under Article 21(1)1 through 3.
(3) A person who intends to report an overseas transfer of marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 22(2) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries a report of overseas transfer of marine and fisheries bioresources, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by the following documents, at least 20 days before the overseas transfer: <Amended on December 3, 2019>
1. Documents concerning the list of marine and fisheries bioresources subject to the report of overseas transfer, the purposes of transfer, and related matters;
2. Documents concerning management plans, including the places and methods of preservation and management following the overseas transfer of marine and fisheries bioresources.
(4) Deleted. <December 3, 2019>

Article 23 (Revocation of Approval for Overseas Transfer and Procedures for Return)
(1) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries revokes approval for overseas transfer under Article 23(1) of the Act, the Minister shall notify the person who obtained the approval of that fact.
(2) A person whose approval for overseas transfer has been revoked under Article 23(1)1 of the Act shall return to the Republic of Korea the marine and fisheries bioresources approved for overseas transfer within 30 days from the date of receipt of the notification under paragraph (1): Provided, That this shall not apply where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries recognizes unavoidable grounds that make return impossible, such as loss of or damage to the marine and fisheries bioresources.
(3) A person who has returned marine and fisheries bioresources to the Republic of Korea pursuant to the main clause of paragraph (2) shall submit documents proving their return to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries within 10 days from the date of return.

Article 24 (Matters and Methods concerning Deposit and Registration, Etc.)
(1) A person who intends to deposit and register marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 24(1) and (2) of the Act shall submit to a responsible agency or a deposit, registration and preservation agency an application for deposit and registration of marine and fisheries bioresources, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by the marine and fisheries bioresources to be deposited and registered and documents detailing the specifications of those marine and fisheries bioresources.
(2) Where a responsible agency or a deposit, registration and preservation agency deems an application for deposit and registration under paragraph (1) appropriate, it shall issue to the applicant a certificate confirming the deposit and registration.
(3) Where a person carrying out a national research and development project concerning marine and fisheries bioresources deposits and registers marine and fisheries bioresources pursuant to the main clause of Article 24(2) of the Act, the person shall, within three months from the date on which the national research and development project ends, consult with the head of the responsible agency on the place and timing of deposit and other matters, and then deposit and register the resources with the responsible agency.
(4) The term "grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 24(2) of the Act means the following grounds:
1. Where the resources are marine and fisheries bioresources requiring special protection under domestic statutes and regulations, international treaties, or the like;
2. Where deposit and registration are inappropriate in light of the characteristics, form, quantity, and other features of the marine and fisheries bioresources produced as a result of carrying out a national research and development project;
3. Where it is necessary to temporarily restrict disclosure in order to file a patent application.

CHAPTER IV ESTABLISHMENT OF INFRASTRUCTURE FOR MARINE AND FISHERIES BIORESOURCES

Article 25 (Establishment and Operation of the Integrated Information System for Marine and Fisheries Bioresources)
Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries establishes and operates an integrated information system concerning marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 27(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "integrated information system for marine and fisheries bioresources"), the Minister shall ensure that it is linked to the integrated information system for biological research resources of the National Biological Research Resources Information Center under Article 11(2)1 of the Act on the Securing, Management and Utilization of Biological Research Resources.

Article 26 (Support for Technology Development and Promotion of Use Relating to Marine and Fisheries Bioresources, Etc.)
(1) The term "matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 31(1)7 of the Act means the following matters:
1. Protection, transfer, utilization, and other matters concerning technologies relating to marine and fisheries bioresources;
2. Development of industries relating to marine and fisheries bioresources;
3. Market research concerning the use of marine and fisheries bioresources.
(2) A person who intends to receive government support under Article 31(2) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries an application for support, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by the following documents:
1. A business plan;
2. A detailed calculation of the required expenses;
3. Records of technology development and utilization relating to marine and fisheries bioresources.
(3) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries deems an application for support under paragraph (2) justified, the Minister shall determine the scale, methods, and conditions of support and other relevant matters and notify the applicant thereof.
(4) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries deems it necessary to manage and supervise the funds provided under paragraph (3), the Minister may request the recipient of the support to submit materials concerning the results of business operations, details of expenditures, or other matters.

Article 27 (Promotion of Research and Development of Overseas Marine and Fisheries Bioresources and International Cooperation, Etc.)
(1) The term "matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 32(1)5 of the Act means matters concerning the conclusion of agreements with foreign governments for international cooperation on marine and fisheries bioresources.
(2) A person who intends to receive government support under Article 32(2) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries an application for support, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by the following documents:
1. A business plan;
2. A detailed calculation of the required expenses;
3. Records of technology development and international cooperation relating to marine and fisheries bioresources.
(3) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries deems an application under paragraph (2) justified, the Minister shall determine the scale, methods, and conditions of support and other relevant matters and notify the applicant thereof.
(4) Where the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries deems it necessary to manage and supervise the funds provided under paragraph (3), the Minister may request the recipient of the support to submit materials concerning the results of business operations, details of expenditures, or other matters.
