Article 28 (Content of Statistics and Publications)
The Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall include the following content in statistics and publications relating to marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 33(1) of the Act:
1. Types of marine and fisheries bioresources and the status of holdings thereof;
2. Institutions holding marine and fisheries bioresources;
3. Specialized personnel relating to marine and fisheries bioresources;
4. Facilities and equipment relating to marine and fisheries bioresources;
5. International trends relating to marine and fisheries bioresources;
6. Policies and systems relating to marine and fisheries bioresources.

CHAPTER V SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS

Article 29 (Delegation and Entrustment of Authority, Etc.)
(1) Pursuant to Article 39(1) of the Act, the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall delegate to the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard the authority to order vessels to stop, conduct searches, seize vessels, and issue other orders or take other measures under Article 13(2) of the Act. <Amended on July 26, 2017>
(2) Pursuant to Article 39(1) of the Act, the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall delegate the following authority, limited to fisheries bioresources among marine and fisheries bioresources, to the head of the National Institute of Fisheries Science: <Amended on March 30, 2021>
1. Conducting basic surveys and detailed surveys of marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 7(1) and (2) of the Act;
2. Surveying the status of and collecting marine and fisheries bioresources and compiling an inventory of marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 9(1) and (3) of the Act;
3. Analyzing and evaluating marine and fisheries bioresources and disclosing the results thereof under Article 10(1) and (2) of the Act;
4. Assigning grades to marine and fisheries bioresources and publicly announcing such assignments under Article 10(1) of the Act and Article 6(2) of this Decree;
4-2. Granting distribution approval and approval for changes in use under Article 20(1) and (3) of the Act;
4-3. Revoking distribution approval and taking measures concerning the return of marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 21(1) of the Act;
5. Establishing and operating the integrated information system for marine and fisheries bioresources and requesting the submission of materials under Article 27(1) and (2) of the Act;
6. Issuing statistics and publications relating to marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 33(1) of the Act.
(3) Pursuant to Article 39(2) of the Act, the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall entrust the following functions, limited to marine bioresources among marine and fisheries bioresources, to the head of the National Marine Biodiversity Institute of Korea: <Amended on March 30, 2021>
1. Conducting basic surveys and detailed surveys of marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 7(1) and (2) of the Act;
2. Surveying the status of and collecting marine and fisheries bioresources and compiling an inventory of marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 9(1) and (3) of the Act;
3. Analyzing and evaluating marine and fisheries bioresources and disclosing the results thereof under Article 10(1) and (2) of the Act;
4. Assigning grades to marine and fisheries bioresources and publicly announcing such assignments under Article 10(1) of the Act and Article 6(2) of this Decree;
5. Establishing and operating the integrated information system for marine and fisheries bioresources and requesting the submission of materials under Article 27(1) and (2) of the Act;
6. Issuing statistics and publications relating to marine and fisheries bioresources under Article 33(1) of the Act;
7. Receiving applications for distribution approval under Article 18(1) and examining whether the criteria for distribution approval under paragraph (2) of that Article are met;
8. Reviewing whether the criteria for approval for changes in use under Article 19(1) are met and receiving applications for approval for changes in use under paragraph (2) of that Article.

